Author: thesa <thesa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 13 21:09:27 2026 -0400

    feat(weather_markets,tracker): var-split bias-correction for the live ensemble blend
    
    Investigation traced the pinned "ensemble" method's condition_type=below
    weakness to gfs_seamless running a persistent +4.4F warm bias on daily-high
    forecasts specifically (min-temp forecasts are fine) -- confirmed via a
    leave-one-out backtest that reweighting the blend by var-split MAE doesn't
    help, but subtracting each model's own signed bias, split by var and never
    pooled across max/min, does (pooling was worse than no correction at all).
    
    Adds tracker.get_member_bias() (signed bias per model+var+city, mirrors
    get_member_accuracy()'s shape) and weather_markets._model_bias() (city ->
    global -> 0.0-if-thin fallback, never pooled-across-var), wired into both
    get_ensemble_temps() and batch_prewarm_ensemble() -- the raw per-model
    cache entries other consumers (_get_consensus_probs, _get_gem_ukmo_means,
    accuracy tracking) read stay uncorrected; only the blended forecast that
    prices trades is bias-corrected.
    
    Also adds backfill_ensemble_member_scores_var() (+ `backfill-ensemble-var`
    CLI command) to recover the var label on historical ensemble_member_scores
    rows logged before call sites passed it, via tracker.predictions' own
    ticker prefix -- most of that table's var-split history didn't exist until
    this backfill ran.
    
    Independent opus review caught 1 critical + 4 minor issues before this
    shipped, all fixed: the backfill's naive version crashed on live data (18
    pre-existing duplicate NULL-var rows collide with idx_ems_dedup once
    resolved to a concrete var, and the single-transaction rollback discarded
    every already-applied update in the same run -- fixed with per-row
    IntegrityError handling, tracked as a new duplicate_conflict return value);
    zero test coverage of batch_prewarm_ensemble (the actual production path)
    despite it being the highest-risk untested line; the bias cache key
    omitted its own floor parameters; a hand-rolled ticker-prefix check
    duplicated the codebase's existing single-source-of-truth
    _var_from_ticker_prefix(); an hourly-market edge case now documented.
    Both the critical fix and the cache-key fix were hand-mutation-tested
    (reverted, confirmed the new tests catch the exact regression, restored).
    
    Backfill run live against predictions.db (backed up first): 220 rows
    recovered, 43 unresolved (no matching prediction/genuinely ambiguous), 6
    duplicate-conflict. gfs_seamless went from 19 to 74 var-tagged rows.
    
    30 new tests; 648 passed/4 skipped across the full test_tracker.py +
    test_weather_markets.py regression scope; ruff/ruff-format/mypy clean via
    the real pre-commit hook.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

